# What stays out of the published archive.
#
# **This file REPLACES .gitignore for publishing — it does not add to it.** That
# is the trap: `__pycache__/` was ignored by git, so it never reached the
# repository, and it still shipped inside 0.2.0 because this file did not repeat
# the rule. Anything that should be absent from the archive has to be listed
# here even if git already ignores it.

# The benchmark charts. The README points at them through absolute
# raw.githubusercontent URLs, so pub.dev renders them without the archive
# carrying 390 kB of PNG that nobody downloading the package will open.
doc/

# Python bytecode, left behind by importing tool/blue_noise.py.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Encoder output from a benchmark or example run.
*.gif

# Editor, agent and OS scratch.
.idea/
*.iml
.vscode/
.codegraph
.claude
.codex
.agents
CLAUDE.md
AGENTS.md
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
